; A page's environments, in the language. A heading's environment is a
; child of the heading above it: a new frame whose parent is that
; environment, so a name defined in a section is seen by the sections
; inside it and by nobody beside it. An environment is a list of frames,
; a frame is (%f . bindings) (see new-frame in cek.vau), and a child is
; a frame in front: nothing the host needs to know. It needs only
; core.vau, so a page can run on a ground that never loaded the
; machine-in-the-language.

($define! child-env
  ($lambda (parent) (cons (cons ($quote %f) ()) parent)))
